---
import BlogLayout from "../../../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";
import ArticleImage from "../../../../components/ui/ArticleImage.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../../../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro";
---

<BlogLayout
  title="What Is an ITIN Loan and How Does It Work? | Cliffco Mortgage"
  description="An ITIN loan allows non-US citizens without a Social Security number to buy a home in America. How it works, who qualifies, and what the process looks like."
  type="article"
>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", href: "/mortgage-guides/blog/" },
    { name: "What Is an ITIN Loan?", href: "/mortgage-guides/blog/what-is-an-itin-loan/" },
  ]} />

  <article class="container-prose pt-12 pb-16">

    <h1 style="font-size: var(--text-display-lg);">What an ITIN Loan Is and How It Works</h1>

    <ArticleImage />

    <p class="mt-8 font-bold">For the Non-Citizen Who Didn't Know Homeownership Was an Option</p>

    <p class="mt-4">If you live and work in the United States, pay taxes, and have been told or assumed that buying a home isn't possible without a Social Security number or a green card, this article is written for you. An ITIN loan is a mortgage product specifically designed for people in your situation.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">The Product Most Lenders Don't Talk About</h2>

    <p class="mt-4">An ITIN loan is a mortgage that uses your Individual Taxpayer Identification Number in place of a Social Security number to verify your identity and tax history. The IRS issues ITINs to individuals who have a tax filing obligation in the United States but are not eligible for a Social Security number. If you've been filing US taxes using an ITIN, you may already have the foundation for a mortgage application, even without citizenship, permanent residency, or a green card.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">The Hidden Gap: Conventional Lending Requires What Most Non-Citizens Don't Have</h2>

    <p class="mt-4">Conventional mortgage programs backed by Fannie Mae and Freddie Mac require a valid Social Security number. That requirement alone disqualifies a significant portion of the non-citizen population who live, work, and pay taxes in the US and have done so for years. ITIN loans exist outside that framework. They are Non-QM products offered by lenders who have built underwriting guidelines specifically for borrowers whose identity documentation doesn't fit the conventional mold.</p>

    <p class="mt-4">Down payment requirements are generally higher than conventional loans, typically starting at 15 to 20% and sometimes more depending on the lender and the borrower's credit profile. Rates run higher than conventional rates, reflecting the Non-QM designation and the additional documentation complexity. Most programs also require at least two years of US tax filings using the ITIN before qualifying.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">How ITIN Loans Are Underwritten</h2>

    <p class="mt-4">Without a Social Security number, the lender builds the borrower's financial profile from a different set of documents. Most ITIN loan programs require two years of tax returns filed with the ITIN, proof of current employment or self-employment income, 12 to 24 months of bank statements, and documentation of any existing credit history in the US.</p>

    <p class="mt-4">Some non-citizens have established US credit through secured cards, auto loans, or other credit products over the years. Others have strong credit histories in their home countries but no US credit file at all. Lenders who specialize in ITIN loans have different approaches to thin or non-existent US credit, some accepting alternative credit documentation such as rental payment history, utility payments, and remittance records in place of a traditional credit score.</p>

    <p class="mt-4">The property itself must be the borrower's primary residence for most ITIN loan programs. Investment property purchases under an ITIN loan are available through some lenders but less common and typically come with stricter requirements.</p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">What to Do, In Order</h2>

    <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Confirm you have an active ITIN and at least two years of US tax filings using it.</strong> Those two elements are the foundation of most ITIN loan programs. If you have less than two years of filings, ask lenders whether any programs accommodate a shorter history.</li>
      <li><strong>Pull together your last two years of tax returns, 12 to 24 months of bank statements, and any documentation of US credit history.</strong> Knowing what you have before you apply gives you a clear picture of where your application is strong and where it needs support.</li>
      <li><strong>Check whether you have any established US credit.</strong> If you don't, ask your lender how they handle alternative credit documentation. Some programs will accept a history of on-time rent payments, utility bills, or other recurring obligations in place of a traditional credit report.</li>
      <li><strong>Work with a lender who has direct experience with ITIN loans.</strong> A lender who regularly closes ITIN loans knows how to structure the documentation and navigate the underwriting process in a way that a general lender does not.</li>
      <li><strong>Plan for a higher down payment than you might expect for a conventional loan.</strong> ITIN loan programs typically require 15 to 20% or more. Build that into your savings target before you start looking at properties.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Find Out What You Qualify For</h2>

    <p class="mt-4">Use Cliffco's Mortgage Readiness Checkup below to see where your application currently stands and what your next step should be. Understanding what you have before you apply makes the process significantly smoother.</p>

    <!-- Embedded lite Mortgage Readiness Checkup -->
    <div class="mt-12 border border-[var(--color-accent)]/25 rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
      <div class="bg-[var(--color-accent)]/8 px-6 py-5 border-b border-[var(--color-accent)]/15">
        <p class="eyebrow text-xs mb-1">Quick check</p>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[var(--color-ink)]">Check your mortgage readiness.</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-1">Answer five questions to see where you stand and what your next move should be.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="p-6">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-1">Credit score range</label>
            <select id="art-mr-credit" class="art-calc-input">
              <option value="780">760 or above</option>
              <option value="740">720 – 759</option>
              <option value="700" selected>680 – 719</option>
              <option value="660">640 – 679</option>
              <option value="630">620 – 639</option>
              <option value="580">Below 620</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-1">Employment type</label>
            <select id="art-mr-emp" class="art-calc-input">
              <option value="w2">W-2 employee</option>
              <option value="self">Self-employed</option>
              <option value="1099">1099 / freelance</option>
              <option value="other">Other / retired</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-1">Gross monthly income ($)</label>
            <input id="art-mr-income" type="number" value="8000" min="0" step="500" class="art-calc-input" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-1">Monthly debt payments ($)</label>
            <input id="art-mr-debt" type="number" value="500" min="0" step="50" class="art-calc-input" />
            <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-1">Car, student loans, credit cards, etc.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-ink)] mb-1">Liquid savings ($)</label>
            <input id="art-mr-savings" type="number" value="20000" min="0" step="1000" class="art-calc-input" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <button id="art-mr-btn" class="btn btn-primary mt-5">Check My Readiness</button>

        <div id="art-mr-result" class="hidden mt-6">
          <div class="p-5 bg-[var(--color-mist-gray)] rounded-lg">
            <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
              <div>
                <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wide">Readiness Level</p>
                <p id="art-mr-level" class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-1"></p>
              </div>
              <div>
                <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] uppercase tracking-wide">Available Housing Budget</p>
                <p id="art-mr-budget" class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-ink)] mt-1"></p>
                <p class="text-xs text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-1">per month (after existing debts)</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div id="art-mr-steps" class="mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] leading-relaxed"></div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 p-5 bg-[var(--color-rich-black)] rounded-lg flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center gap-4 justify-between">
            <div>
              <p class="text-white font-semibold">Ready to move forward?</p>
              <p class="text-white/70 text-sm mt-1">A Cliffco loan officer will give you a real pre-approval - not just an estimate.</p>
            </div>
            <a href="/get-started/" class="btn btn-primary !bg-white !text-[var(--color-rich-black)] shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap">Talk to a loan officer</a>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-center text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
            Want to model other scenarios? <a href="/mortgage-guides/calculators/mortgage-readiness/" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] font-medium">View the full mortgage readiness checkup →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </article>
</BlogLayout>

<style>
  .art-calc-input {
    width: 100%;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-soft-gray, #d1d5db);
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    background: white;
    outline: none;
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .art-calc-input:focus {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) 15%, transparent);
  }
</style>

<script>
  const mrBtn = document.getElementById("art-mr-btn")!;
  mrBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
    const credit = +(document.getElementById("art-mr-credit") as HTMLSelectElement).value;
    const emp = (document.getElementById("art-mr-emp") as HTMLSelectElement).value;
    const income = +(document.getElementById("art-mr-income") as HTMLInputElement).value;
    const debt = +(document.getElementById("art-mr-debt") as HTMLInputElement).value;
    const savings = +(document.getElementById("art-mr-savings") as HTMLInputElement).value;

    const maxDTI = credit >= 720 ? 0.45 : credit >= 660 ? 0.43 : 0.41;
    const availableForHousing = Math.max(0, income * maxDTI - debt);
    const fmt = (v: number) => "$" + Math.round(v).toLocaleString("en-US");

    let level = "";
    let steps: string[] = [];

    if (credit < 620) {
      level = "Not Yet Ready";
      steps = ["Your credit score needs to reach at least 620 before most lenders will approve a mortgage.", "Focus on paying down balances and removing errors from your credit report.", "Contact a Cliffco loan officer for a personalized credit improvement plan."];
    } else if (savings < 10000) {
      level = "Building";
      steps = ["You'll need more savings to cover a down payment and closing costs.", "Down payment programs may help if you're a first-time buyer.", "A Cliffco loan officer can show you what down payment assistance programs you qualify for."];
    } else if (emp === "self" || emp === "1099" || emp === "other") {
      level = "Ready (Non-QM Path)";
      steps = ["Your income type may not qualify for conventional financing.", "Non-QM loan programs (bank statement, 1099, DSCR) were built for your situation.", "Talk to a Cliffco Non-QM specialist to identify the best product."];
    } else if (credit >= 720 && availableForHousing > 1500) {
      level = "Strong";
      steps = ["You're in a solid position. Get pre-approved before you start shopping.", "Keep your credit stable, avoid new debt, and gather two years of tax returns.", "A pre-approval will tell you exactly what purchase price you qualify for."];
    } else {
      level = "Ready";
      steps = ["You have the foundation to move forward.", "Ask your loan officer about the right loan program for your credit and income.", "Getting pre-approved now puts you in the strongest position when you find the right home."];
    }

    (document.getElementById("art-mr-level") as HTMLElement).textContent = level;
    (document.getElementById("art-mr-budget") as HTMLElement).textContent = fmt(availableForHousing);
    (document.getElementById("art-mr-steps") as HTMLElement).innerHTML =
      "<strong>Your next steps:</strong><ul class='list-disc list-inside mt-2 space-y-1'>" +
      steps.map(s => `<li>${s}</li>`).join("") + "</ul>";
    (document.getElementById("art-mr-result") as HTMLElement).classList.remove("hidden");
  });
</script>
